  #### Step 1: Set your real crypto wallet addresses                                                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                                                                      
  Open wallets.json (or wallets.json) and replace the placeholder 0x000... and bc1q... addresses with your actual receiving wallet addresses for BSC, Ethereum, Bitcoin, Polygon,     
  Base, and Arbitrum.                                                                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                                      
  #### Step 2: Download Firebase Service Account credentials                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                      
  1. Go to Firebase Console https://console.firebase.google.com/ → vectorizerr → Project Settings → Service accounts.                                                                 
  2. Click Generate new private key (downloads a .json file).                                                                                                                         
  3. From this file, note client_email and private_key.                                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                      
  #### Step 3: Run / Deploy the Cloudflare Worker Backend
  
  1. Local test:
    cd backend
    cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
    # Paste your FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL and FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY into .dev.vars
    npm run dev
  
  2. Deploy to Cloudflare:
    cd backend
    npx wrangler secret put FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL
    npx wrangler secret put FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY
    npm run deploy
  Wrangler will output your live worker URL (e.g. https://vectorizerr-backend.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev).
  
  #### Step 4: Connect the Worker URL to the Frontend
  
  In frontend/.env.local (and in your Cloudflare Pages dashboard):
  
    NEXT_PUBLIC_REFRESH_CREDITS_FUNCTION_URL=https://vectorizerr-backend.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/api/refresh-credits
  
  #### Step 5: Deploy the updated Firestore Security Rules
  
  Deploy the updated firestore.rules to lock down credits and enforce server-only authorization:
  
    cd frontend
    firebase deploy --only firestore:rules
  
  #### Step 6: Enable Firebase App Check
  
  1. In Firebase Console, go to App Check → Apps → select your Web App.
  2. Select reCAPTCHA v3 or Enterprise, paste your secret key, and copy the public site key into NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY.
  3. For local debugging, open your browser DevTools console on localhost:3000 to view the App Check debug token, and paste it into App Check → Manage debug tokens in Firebase       
  Console.